// Criterion: non-pointer types can also be compared against `None` -- `None` in pathspace means
// "no value", independent of the slot's type.
// Reference: 03-type-system/03-kinds-codes-and-special-values.kv ("None criterion").
//
// Isolates **non-pointer `None` comparison** (hence `none_comparison`, renamed from `dynamic_key_none`
// which did not actually exercise dynamic keys).
//
// Uses an **existing absolute key**: value is present, so `== None` is `false`. The four paired cases
// (zero local / present key / null pointer / `!=` counterparts) are in `member/nonnull_test.kv`.
//
// **Dynamic-key carrier pending #634**: once `m·*k` (`0x4107` VALUE_ACCESS) lands, add a dedicated
// dynamic-member `None` test rather than mixing two independent features here.
//
// Expected output:
//   false
//   true

rwfunc test() -> () {
	/existing:int64 = 7
	v:int64 = /existing
	println(v == None)
	println(v != None)
}
